.nh
.TH "ORBIT" "1" "Aug 2026" "Orbit Developer Platform" "Orbit Platform Manual"

.SH NAME
orbit-dev-tunnel - Forward the shared dev services over SSH to 127.0.0.1


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBorbit dev tunnel [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Forward every registry service and exception with runs: shared (ports.yaml) from the dev tunnel host to 127.0.0.1 with ssh -L. The host comes from --host or dev.tunnel_host, the SSH port from --ssh-port or dev.tunnel_port. The command runs in the foreground; Ctrl-C ends it. --print shows the ssh command, --ssh-config prints a Host block for ~/.ssh/config, --authorized-key prints the server-side authorized_keys line for a public key file, and --json prints the plan.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--authorized-key\fP=""
	print the server authorized_keys line for this ssh public key file (.pub)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for tunnel

.PP
\fB--host\fP=""
	SSH destination user@host (default: dev.tunnel_host)

.PP
\fB--identity\fP=""
	private key file for the tunnel, passed as ssh -i (default: dev.tunnel_identity; ~ expands to your home)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print the tunnel plan (host, port, forwards, command) as a JSON envelope and do not run ssh

.PP
\fB--only\fP=[]
	forward only these registry service names, comma separated

.PP
\fB--print\fP[=false]
	print the ssh command and exit

.PP
\fB--root\fP=""
	workspace root holding handbook/agents/workspace/ports.yaml (default: the workspace containing the current directory)

.PP
\fB--ssh-config\fP[=false]
	print a Host orbit-dev block for ~/.ssh/config and exit

.PP
\fB--ssh-port\fP=0
	SSH port of the tunnel host (default: dev.tunnel_port)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	Custom path to Orbit CLI configuration file


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBorbit-dev(1)\fP
